Give every domain its own test package

ProjecturedDomainTest is gone, and with it the last package/domain directory.
Each domain's suites live in package/<domain>/test/ behind a test_<domain>()
aggregator that also runs that package's layering guard.

The umbrella keeps every suite whose fixture names several domains — which is
most of what was left: ConstructTest builds JSON, YAML and XML; the table,
dragging, insertion, gesture and serializer suites all mix domains; the Console
and Pdf backend tests drive a JSON pipeline but need the umbrella's graphics
example. test_domain_examples() moves here too, because the registry it walks
names factories from all twenty example packages.

Four things had to move or change beyond the plain split:

- test_xml_parser lived in JsonParserTest. It is now xml/test/document/XmlParserTest.jl.
- The conversation panel, parsing and serialization suites drive
  WorkbenchAssistant, so they rose to the umbrella rather than pull workbench
  into the conversation test package.
- WorkbenchFileTest needs the gallery's window helpers, so it rose too.
- Six aggregators collided with a suite of the same name — test_json, test_fsm,
  test_graph, test_process, test_chart, test_sequencechart. The file-level suite
  took a more specific name (test_json_document, test_graph_projection, …) and
  the bare name is now the package aggregator, which is what a reader expects it
  to mean. test_database collided with the ODBC live-connection suite, so the
  domain one is test_database_domain.

Every domain guide moved to its package's doc/. versioning.md went to base,
where the code already lives. The old domain architecture guide is now
documentation/domains.md and still describes the dissolved package; the
documentation pass rewrites it.

Verified: all twenty test packages green — 2261 pass, 1 broken, 0 fail, 0 error.
The suites that rose to the umbrella pass too.
